Please perform a careful analysis of the telemetry window in `data/imu_2026-09-14.csv` and the implementation in `firmware/src/TelemetryRing.cpp`. The result is for a design review, so separate numerical findings, code-level causes, and recommendations. The MCU is an STM32H743 sampling three axes at 2 kHz. DMA writes 256 `Sample` objects into a ring, and the consumer sends batches of 64 over CAN-FD. We saw 37 missing sequence numbers in a 19-minute capture, but no watchdog reset. The producer and consumer run at different interrupt priorities, and D-cache is enabled.

Relevant code from `firmware/src/TelemetryRing.cpp`:
```cpp
struct Sample { uint32_t seq; int16_t x, y, z; };
alignas(32) volatile Sample dma_ring[256];
volatile uint16_t write_idx = 0;
volatile uint16_t read_idx = 0;

void on_dma_half_complete() {
    write_idx += 128;
    ready = true;
}

void drain() {
    while (read_idx != write_idx) {
        auto s = dma_ring[read_idx & 0xff];
        send_can(s);
        ++read_idx;
    }
}
```

